  "question": {
    "text": "The locus of a point $P(\\alpha, \\beta)$ moving under the condition that the line $y=\\alpha x+\\beta$ is a tangent to the hyperbola $\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "Hr1DA",
      "text": "\nan ellipse\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "qAiGA",
      "text": "\na circle\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Vy0Ab",
      "text": "\na parabola\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "WwnJG",
      "text": "\na hyperbola",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Tangent to the hyperbola $\\frac{x^2}{a^2}-\\frac{y^2}{b^2}=1$ is\n$y=m x \\pm \\sqrt{a^2 m^2-b^2}$\nGiven that $y=\\alpha x+\\beta$ is the tangent of hyperbola\n$\\Rightarrow m=\\alpha$ and $a^2 m^2-b^2=\\beta^2$\n$\\therefore \\mathrm{a}^2 \\alpha^2-\\mathrm{b}^2=\\beta^2$\nLocus is $a^2 x^2-y^2=b^2$ which is hyperbola.",
    "image": null
  },
